+// [openbf2] Where a stroke run itself begins.
+//
+// A stroke without a fill is closed only when it comes back to **its own**
+// first point. Comparing against `fill_start` — the last `moveTo` of the
+// whole drawing — closes runs that merely end where some earlier subpath
+// began, and `close()` then draws a segment across the shape.
+//
+// BF2's menu hits this on every button: the bevel is drawn as
+// `moveTo(100,0) lineTo(0,0) lineTo(0,100)`, then `lineStyle` starts a
+// second run at (0,100) which ends back at (100,0). That run was being
+// closed, and the connecting segment showed up as a diagonal across each
+// button and input field (docs/research/11-ruffle-menu.md).
+fn line_run_start(line: &DrawingLine) -> Option<Point<Twips>> {
+    match line.commands.first() {
+        Some(DrawCommand::MoveTo(point)) => Some(*point),
+        _ => None,
+    }
+}
